{{ProjectName}} is a sample command-line tool built from the go/cli
template. It demonstrates the CLI contract: data goes to stdout,
diagnostics go to stderr, and the command surface (flags, output
schema, exit codes) is a tested API.

Exit codes:
  0  success
  1  failure (the command ran but could not complete)
  2  usage error (unknown command, bad flags, invalid arguments)

Configuration precedence: flags, then environment
(<PREFIX>_FORMAT and friends, where the prefix is the
upper-cased tool name), then defaults. Secrets are read from
the environment, never from flags.

Usage:
  {{project-name}} [command]

Available Commands:
  completion  Generate the autocompletion script for the specified shell
  help        Help about any command
  text        Text transformations

Flags:
      --dry-run         show what would happen without writing anything
      --format string   output format: plain or json (default "plain")
  -h, --help            help for {{project-name}}
      --json            shorthand for --format json
      --no-color        disable color in diagnostics (NO_COLOR is also honoured)
      --no-input        never prompt; fail instead of asking
      --quiet           suppress diagnostics
      --verbose         print diagnostics about what the command is doing
  -v, --version         version for {{project-name}}

Use "{{project-name}} [command] --help" for more information about a command.
